    1$; that signal is above $1 \/ 2$ and survives every subsequent step.
    Wherever $parallel pi \( b \) parallel > 1 \/ 2$, the initial ramp has $parallel pi \( y_0 \) parallel = 1$.
    If $parallel pi \( y_(j - 1) \) parallel = 1$, its copy under $theta_j$ has norm one,
